    "description": "Offsets and length are bytes. Negative offset uses zero, absent length means the rest, and a nonpositive length produces an empty String.\n\nOffsets and length are bytes. Negative offset uses zero, absent length means the rest, and a nonpositive length produces an empty String.\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: frog.studio.string.raw-bytes@1.\nExpected:\nresult (string) = \"\"\n",
